  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 141 PM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nHigh pressure will remain in control of the pattern through the end \nof the week, continuing our hot and dry weather. The HeatRisk will \nremain moderate to major, with isolated locations experiencing an \nextreme HeatRisk. With no significant shift in the pattern, have \nused the observed forecast dewpoints as guidance for 04Z-19Z \nThursday as models continue to forecast values a bit higher than \nrecent observations. Based on this, it looks like a heat advisory \nwill not be necessary for Thursday, though isolated locations could \nhave heat index values around 110. Moisture will likely return this \nweekend, returning the need for Heat Advisories. Folks spending time \noutdoors this weekend should practice heat safety as heat index \nvalues of 110+ will be likely along the inland Coastal Bend. \n\nThe forecast begins to get a little murky by Sunday as the trailing \nedge of mid-level trough to our northeast moves across the eastern \nperiphery of the high pressure. This could introduce a few showers \nacross South Texas, with the main focus over the Victoria Crossroads \nand Coastal Bend.",
